summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q96G46","text":"Catalyzes the synthesis of dihydrouridine, a modified base, in various RNAs, such as tRNAs, mRNAs and some long non-coding RNAs (lncRNAs) (PubMed:34556860). Mainly modifies the uridine in position 47 (U47) in the D-loop of most cytoplasmic tRNAs (PubMed:34556860). Also able to mediate the formation of dihydrouridine in some mRNAs, thereby regulating their translation (PubMed:34556860)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}